NAME
       stat - display file status

SYNOPSIS
       stat [-t] file ...

DESCRIPTION
       Prints the size, type, mode, owner and timestamps of each FILE.

OPTIONS
       -t     terse: one line per file, fields separated by spaces

NOTES
       Access, Modify and Change are printed in full where the
       filesystem records them. ext2, ext4, FAT32, ISO 9660, UDF, 9P
       and the initramfs all do; /dev and /proc report the boot time.

SEE ALSO
       ls(1), touch(1)
